  "error_identification": "Turn 1 missing tool calls: the model's turn 1 output includes wc operations that are either not present in ground truth or were not properly tracked in the execution response chain. The model generated 6 wc calls but the ground truth execution results for turn 1 appear to expect a different set of operations.",
  "root_cause_analysis": "The model over-executed file analysis operations in turn 1 by calling wc with all three modes (lines, words, characters) for both files sequentially. This violates delta11 (execute required transformations directly per turn) and delta14 (never chain multiple operations of the same type in one turn). The ground truth likely expects a single atomic diff operation or a more constrained set of file operations.",
  "correct_approach": "In turn 1, execute only the diff operation directly without chaining multiple wc calls. Per delta11, commit to the exact tool needed for the comparison task (diff) and yield immediately after tool output. Reserve wc operations for separate turns if explicitly requested, rather than proactively chaining them.",
  "key_insight": "Multi-turn file comparison tasks should execute one atomic operation per turn (diff for comparison) rather than supplementing with exploratory wc chains. The model's anticipatory analysis, while contextually helpful, violated the constraint that tool execution must match ground truth state mutations exactly."
